# Machine-local GPU policy

Save as `infra/gpu_policy.md` after configuring the current server.

- Scheduler/cluster: `<SLURM_CLUSTER_OR_OTHER_APPROVED_BACKEND>`.
- Authorized partitions/nodes: `<LOCAL_ALLOWLIST>`.
- Concurrent GPU limit: `<EXPLICIT_AUTHORIZED_LIMIT>`.
- Remaining experiment budget: read the active plan and preserved accounting;
  a server move does not reset the budget.
- Per-node CPU, host-memory and walltime limits: `<LOCAL_LIMITS>`.
- Dataset/model/cache locations: use this server's `ACCESS_POLICY.md`.
- GPU work must use the approved scheduler, never the login node.
- Bounded CPU-only work follows local server guidance.

Initialize `infra/gpu_scheduler.py` from the tracked example only if Slurm and
its supported GPU types match this server. Fill its topology and memory tables;
review its type-specific scheduling behavior. For another backend, supply an
appropriate local adapter. Never submit with another server's node names.

Use project-local uv environments. Validate package/model revisions, image
processing, scheduling and reproducibility before resuming scientific inference.
Existing run configurations may contain old paths/node settings; resolve them
under a documented execution amendment without changing frozen science.

Use suitable job walltimes (typically 24–48 hours for long runs where allowed),
but enforce the experiment's actual cumulative GPU-hour ceiling separately.
A longer walltime is not permission to spend more GPU-hours. No keeper/idle job.
